s($,"aEP","aq1",()=>A.aJ(["Abu Dhabi",A.pz("Sheikh Mohamed bin Zayed Al Nahyan","Abu Dhabi, the largest emirate by area, was founded in the mid-18th century by the Bani Yas tribe led by the Al Nahyan family. It covers about 67,340 square kilometers and has a population of around 1.5 million. Geographically, it features vast deserts, islands, and a long coastline along the Arabian Gulf.","Oil wealth and cultural heritage","The Sheikh Zayed Grand Mosque, an architectural masterpiece, and the Louvre Abu Dhabi, a world-class museum, are key landmarks. The emirate also features the Corniche waterfront and Yas Island with its Formula 1 circuit."),"Dubai",A.pz("Sheikh Mohammed bin Rashid Al Maktoum","Dubai, founded in the early 19th century by the Al Maktoum family, is the most populous emirate with over 3 million residents. It spans approximately 4,114 square kilometers and is located on the Arabian Gulf coast, known for its desert landscape and urban development.","Tourism and luxury lifestyle","Burj Khalifa, the tallest building in the world, and the Palm Jumeirah, a man-made island shaped like a palm tree, are iconic. Dubai Mall and Dubai Marina are also major attractions."),"Sharjah",A.pz("Sheikh Sultan bin Muhammad Al Qasimi","Sharjah, founded in the 18th century and ruled by the Al Qasimi family, has a population of about 1.4 million and covers roughly 2,590 square kilometers. It lies on the Arabian Gulf coast and is known for its cultural and educational institutions.","Cultural preservation and arts","The Sharjah Museum of Islamic Civilization and Al Noor Mosque are prominent cultural sites. The Heart of Sharjah project aims to preserve the emirate\u2019s heritage."),"Fujairah",A.pz("Sheikh Hamad bin Mohammed Al Sharqi","Fujairah is the only emirate located entirely on the Gulf of Oman coast, covering 1,166 square kilometers with a population of about 250,000. It has a mountainous terrain and a history rooted in fishing and trade.","Beaches and historical sites","Fujairah Fort and Al Bidya Mosque, the oldest mosque in the UAE, are important historical sites. The emirate is also known for its beaches and diving spots."),"Ajman",A.pz("Sheikh Humaid bin Rashid Al Nuaimi","Ajman is the smallest emirate, covering just 260 square kilometers, with a population of around 500,000. Founded in the early 19th century, it is located on the Arabian Gulf coast and has a mix of urban and coastal geography.","Traditional crafts and coastal charm","Ajman Fort and Ajman Museum highlight the emirate\u2019s history. The Ajman Corniche is a popular seaside promenade."),"Umm Al Quwain",A.pz("Sheikh Saud bin Rashid Al Mualla","Umm Al Quwain, one of the least populous emirates with about 72,000 residents, covers 770 square kilometers. It was founded centuries ago and is characterized by its coastal plains and islands along the Arabian Gulf.","Natural landscapes and tranquility","Umm Al Quwain Fort and Dreamland Aqua Park are notable attractions. The emirate is known for its natural mangroves and wildlife reserves."),"Ras Al Khaimah",A.pz("Sheikh Saud bin Saqr Al Qasimi","Ras Al Khaimah, with a population of around 400,000, covers 1,684 square kilometers. It has a rich history dating back thousands of years and features diverse geography including mountains, deserts, and coastline.","Mountains and adventure tourism","Jebel Jais, the highest peak in the UAE, and Dhayah Fort are key landmarks. The emirate also has archaeological sites and beaches.")],t.N,A.a1("vy")))
